  <prompt>
    Implement FR-14: redesign the Compose accept/reject surface so it **leads with the cited
    rationale** as the primary trust cue and treats the `confidence_band` (from task 030) as a
    **secondary** signal — never the headline. Engineer the surface against rubber-stamping per the
    2026 HCI research (design §6.2): low-confidence edits are **NEVER pre-selected or auto-accepted**,
    and every low-band edit exposes an **explicit-review affordance**. "Accept all" MUST NOT include
    low-band edits without an explicit confirmation step. This is a client-only change to the existing
    accept/reject render path in `ComposeEditor.tsx` (`redlineLabelText`, lines 271-294); it consumes
    the additive `confidence_band` field that task 030 added to `ComposeDraftPayload`. Do NOT emit a
    false-precision numeric score, do NOT re-derive the band client-side (it is server-derived), and do
    NOT change the mark/range apply layer.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior React + Fluent UI v9 engineer building trustworthy AI-assist surfaces. Fluent in the
    TipTap accept/reject popover pattern, dark-mode-correct Fluent v9 tokens (ADR-021), and HCI
    anti-over-reliance design (rationale-first, no false-precision, no one-click accept-all for
    unverified edits).
  </role>

  <goal>
    An accept/reject surface where the cited rationale is visually primary and the `confidence_band`
    is a secondary, coarse qualitative cue (high/medium/low — never a numeric score); low-confidence
    redlines are never pre-selected or auto-accepted and carry an explicit-review affordance; and
    "accept all" excludes low-band edits unless the user explicitly confirms their inclusion. Built on
    Fluent v9 with correct dark-mode tokens. Component/interaction tests assert the rationale-primary
    ordering, the no-auto-accept-low-band rule, and the accept-all exclusion + confirmation gate.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      E3-rationale already ships: the accept/reject popover renders `rationale` today
      (`ComposeEditor.tsx:271-294`, `redlineLabelText`) — design §2 redline-payload row + §6.1. Task
      030 adds the server-derived `confidence_band` to `ComposeDraftPayload`. The 2026 HCI research
      folded into design §6.2 warns that a numeric confidence score drives over-reliance + false
      precision and that users rubber-stamp more as difficulty rises — so the design is deliberately
      **rationale-first**: lead with why + grounded-in-what; show confidence only as a coarse band;
      and engineer against rubber-stamping (never pre-select/auto-accept low-confidence; no one-click
      accept-all for unverified edits). This task implements those trust semantics in the UI. It does
      NOT compute the band (server does, task 030) and does NOT touch the mark/range apply layer
      (already correct, `usePendingRedline.ts:461-465`).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeEditor.tsx — the accept/reject surface; `redlineLabelText` + popover at lines 271-294. Make the rationale primary; render `confidence_band` as a secondary coarse band; add the explicit-review affordance + accept-all exclusion logic.</file>
      <file role="canonical-reuse">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/types/compose-contracts.ts — consume the `confidence_band` field (mirrored by task 030); do NOT re-derive it client-side.</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/hooks/usePendingRedline.ts — the pending-redline/accept-reject state hook; wire the no-auto-accept + accept-all-excludes-low-band rules here / at the popover, NOT in the mark/range apply layer (461-465, unchanged).</file>
      <file role="design">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r3/design.md §6.2 (rationale-first; confidence as coarse band tied to verifiability; never pre-select/auto-accept low-confidence; explicit-review affordances; no false-precision score), §2 (redline-payload row — rationale already surfaced).</file>
      <file role="spec">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r3/spec.md FR-14, NFR-10 (Fluent v9 + dark mode, `@spaarke/auth`).</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="030" status="pending">FR-13/FR-16 server-derived `confidence_band` + paraId/offsets. Provides the `confidence_band` field on `ComposeDraftPayload` (client mirror) that this UI consumes. Without it there is no band to render or gate on.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-021 / NFR-10">New/changed UI uses Fluent UI v9 components + tokens with correct dark-mode rendering. No inline hex; use design tokens. No Fluent v8 or ad-hoc CSS colors.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / design §6.2">Rationale is the PRIMARY trust cue (visually leads); `confidence_band` is SECONDARY and coarse (high/medium/low) — never a numeric/percentage score (no false precision). Low-confidence edits are NEVER pre-selected or auto-accepted; each exposes an explicit-review affordance. "Accept all" excludes low-band edits unless the user explicitly confirms including them.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / NFR-04">Client-only change; the band is SERVER-DERIVED — do NOT re-derive or synthesize a band client-side, and do NOT add a new AI call or dispatch. Consume the field task 030 provides.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / S5">Do NOT modify the mark/range apply layer (`usePendingRedline.ts:461-465`) — it is already slice-safe. This task is popover/label + selection-gating logic only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028 / NFR-10">Any client fetch uses `@spaarke/auth` (no bespoke token handling). This task is primarily render/interaction; if it reads data it goes through the existing authed path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-06 / ADR-038">Reachability + interaction evidence: the surface must be mounted + reachable in the running host, and the accept-all/no-auto-accept rules asserted by component/interaction tests — not just built in isolation.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Fluent v9 accept/reject popover; rationale-first anti-over-reliance UX; consuming a mirrored server contract field</topic>
