  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + dependency check">Confirm task 030 landed the `confidence_band` mirror on `ComposeDraftPayload`. Run the FULL rigor-level declaration. Load the Fluent v9 + ADR-038 knowledge files.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Make the rationale primary">In `ComposeEditor.tsx` (`redlineLabelText` / popover, 271-294), restructure the accept/reject surface so the cited rationale (+ sources) is the visual headline; render `confidence_band` as a secondary coarse band (high/medium/low), never a numeric/percentage score. Fluent v9 tokens, dark-mode-correct.</step>
    <step order="2" name="No auto-accept / no pre-select of low-band">In the pending-redline selection layer (`usePendingRedline.ts` / popover state), ensure low-confidence redlines are never pre-selected or auto-accepted; add an explicit-review affordance on each low-band edit. Do NOT touch the mark/range apply (461-465).</step>
    <step order="3" name="Accept-all excludes low-band without confirmation">Change "accept all" so it excludes low-band edits by default; including them requires an explicit confirmation step (a deliberate second action), not a silent inclusion.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Component + interaction tests">Author tests asserting: rationale renders above/primary to the band; a low-band redline is not pre-selected and not auto-accepted; "accept all" leaves low-band edits unapplied until explicit confirmation. Assert dark-mode token usage where feasible.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Reachability + verify">Confirm the surface is mounted + reachable in the running host (not isolated). Build the client shared lib; run the tests. Update TASK-INDEX status.</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeEditor.tsx (rationale-first accept/reject surface + secondary band + explicit-review affordance)</output>
