  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">The accept/reject surface leads with the cited rationale as the primary trust cue; the `confidence_band` renders as a secondary coarse band (high/medium/low) — no numeric/percentage confidence score is shown (no false precision).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Low-confidence edits are never pre-selected and never auto-accepted; each low-band edit exposes an explicit-review affordance — asserted by an interaction test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">"Accept all" does not include low-band edits without an explicit confirmation step — asserted by an interaction test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The band is consumed from the server-derived `confidence_band` field (task 030 mirror); the UI does NOT re-derive a band client-side and adds no new AI call.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">New/changed UI uses Fluent v9 + correct dark-mode tokens (ADR-021); the mark/range apply layer (`usePendingRedline.ts:461-465`) is unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The surface is mounted + reachable in the running host; client shared-lib build is green with matching tests passing.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

